\section*{Filtered smash products of cobordism-null restrictions}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Cobordism-null restrictions are claimed to vanish coherently on large constrained smash-product unions, yielding boundary-preserving cube compression under a torus-bundle embedding of rank strictly below twice the source rank. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 302, 2026-09-25): Product filtrations grow linearly while a uniform connective nilpotence cutoff grows sublinearly, forcing stable vanishing across the entire constrained union. Compatible local duality turns the vanishing into avoidance, and radial normalization restores old boundary slots. Padding and a coordinate-preserving polyhedral model remove input-dimension restrictions while retaining a positive boundary fraction.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 302, 2026-09-25): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
